      <!-- Item Summary -->
      <div id="summary" class="section metadataSection">

        
        <div class="section__header sh">
          <h2 class="sh__main">Summary</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="section__content">
          
                      <p class="small">
              <strong>Short Citation</strong><br>
              Office of Coast Survey, 2026: NOAA Electronic Navigational Charts (ENC), https://www.fisheries.noaa.gov/inport/item/39976.<br>
              <a href="/inport/item/39976/citation">Full Citation Examples</a>
            </p>
                    
                                    <strong>Abstract</strong><br>
                        <div class="small">
                    <p>The Office of Coast Survey (OCS) has been involved in the development of a NOAA Electronic Navigational Chart (NOAA ENC) suite to support the marine transportation infrastructure and coastal management for a number of years. The NOAA ENC will support all types of marine navigation by providing the official database for electronic charting systems (ECS), including the Electronic Chart Display and Information System (ECDIS). NOAA ENCs support real-time navigation as well as collision and grounding avoidance needs of the mariner, and accommodate a real-time tide and current display capability that is essential for large vessel navigation.  NOAA ENCs will also provide fully integrated vector base maps for use in geographic information systems (GIS) that are used for coastal management or other purposes. The NOAA ENCs are in the International Hydrographic Office (IHO) S-57 international exchange format and comply with the ENC Product Specification.</p>
              </div>
          
                      <strong>Purpose</strong><br>
            <div class="small">
                    <p>The electronic navigational charts (NOAA ENC) are primarily intended to support the navigation of vessels in the territorial waters of the United States.  The data contained in the NOAA ENCs may also be used for any other coastal mapping purposes that require up-to-date information similar to that portrayed on traditional navigational charts.</p>
              </div>
          
          
          <div class="cf"></div> <!-- needed to clear browse image float -->

          <div class="inner-col-2">
            <div class="inner-col-2__main">

              
              
              
              
              
                              <div class="inner-col-section">
                  <div class="inner-col-section__header inner-col-sh">
                    <h3 class="inner-col-sh__main">Distribution Information</h3>
                  </div>
                  <div class="inner-col-section__content">
                                          <ul class="content-list">
                                                <li>
                          <div class="force-break">
                                                          <a href="https://charts.noaa.gov/ENCs/ENCs.shtml" rel="noopener"
                                 target="_blank">Chart Downloader for NOAA ENCs</a>
                                                      </div>
                                                      <div class="small">
                              2
                            </div>
                                                                                <div class="small">
                                    <p>Individual NOAA ENCs may be downloaded from the Chart Downloader for NOAA ENC. </p>
      <p>The NOAA ENCs distributed here are a geo-referenced database(s) of NOAA nautical chart features and their attributes, published by NOAA in the format of the International Hydrographic Organization S-57 Standard, &quot;IHO Transfer Standard for Digital Hydrographic Data.&quot; NOAA updates the ENCs for Notice to Mariners on a weekly basis (timing of their availability is not guaranteed). NOAA ENCs are an official product of NOAA.</p>
                              </div>
                                                  </li>
                                                <li>
                          <div class="force-break">
                                                          <a href="https://charts.noaa.gov/InteractiveCatalog/nrnc.shtml" rel="noopener"
                                 target="_blank">NOAA Chart Locator </a>
                                                      </div>
                                                                                <div class="small">
                                    <p>Individual NOAA ENCs may be downloaded from the NOAA Chart Locator.</p>
                              </div>
                                                  </li>
                                                <li>
                          <div class="force-break">
                                                          <a href="https://devgis.charttools.noaa.gov/pod" rel="noopener"
                                 target="_blank">NOAA Custom Chart (NCC)</a>
                                                      </div>
                                                      <div class="small">
                              PDF - Adobe Portable Document Format
                            </div>
                                                                                <div class="small">
                                    <p>The NOAA Custom Chart application enables users to create their own customized charts directly from the latest NOAA ENC data. These charts contain all the same information as ENCs, but it is presented using the same symbols and colors used on traditional paper nautical charts. NCC outputs geospatially referenced Portable Document Format (PDF) files</p>
      <p>All recreational and professional mariners are encouraged to use NOAA's premier navigational product, the electronic navigational chart (ENC) for their primary means of navigation. NCC uses the latest up-to-date NOAA ENC data to create customized charts and these charts are especially useful for voyage planning and situational awareness.</p>
                              </div>
                                                  </li>
                                                <li>
                          <div class="force-break">
                                                          <a href="https://gis.charttools.noaa.gov/arcgis/rest/services/MCS/ENCOnline/MapServer/exts/MaritimeChartService/MapServer" rel="noopener"
                                 target="_blank">ECDIS Display Service - REST Service</a>
                                                      </div>
                                                      <div class="small">
                              ESRI REST Service
                            </div>
                                                                                <div class="small">
                                    <p>The ECDIS Display Service uses symbology developed by the International Hydrographic Organization (IHO) for the display of ENC data on Electronic Chart Display and Information Systems (ECDIS) that large ocean- going vessels and many smaller commercial ships use for navigation. This symbol set is commonly referred to by its IHO specification number, &quot;S-52,&quot; or as &quot;ECDIS symbology.&quot; This is the Esri REST service.</p>
                              </div>
                                                  </li>
                                                <li>
                          <div class="force-break">
                                                          <a href="https://gis.charttools.noaa.gov/arcgis/rest/services/MCS/ENCOnline/MapServer/exts/MaritimeChartService/WMSServer" rel="noopener"
                                 target="_blank">ECDIS Display Service </a>
                                                      </div>
                                                      <div class="small">
                              WMS - Web Map Service
                            </div>
                                                                                <div class="small">
                                    <p>The ECDIS Display Service uses symbology developed by the International Hydrographic Organization (IHO) for the display of ENC data on Electronic Chart Display and Information Systems (ECDIS) that large ocean- going vessels and many smaller commercial ships use for navigation. This is the OGC Web Map Service (WMS).</p>
                              </div>
                                                  </li>
                                                <li>
                          <div class="force-break">
                                                          <a href="https://gis.charttools.noaa.gov/arcgis/rest/services/MCS/NOAAChartDisplay/MapServer/exts/MaritimeChartService/MapServer" rel="noopener"
                                 target="_blank">NOAA Chart Display Service (Esri REST Service)</a>
                                                      </div>
                                                      <div class="small">
                              ESRI REST Service
                            </div>
                                                                                <div class="small">
                                    <p>The NOAA Chart Display Service renders NOAA ENC data with &quot;traditional paper chart&quot; symbols, labels, and color schemes familiar to those who have used NOAA paper nautical charts or the NOAA Custom Chart application. This is the Esri REST Service.</p>
                              </div>
                                                  </li>
                                                <li>
                          <div class="force-break">
                                                          <a href="https://gis.charttools.noaa.gov/arcgis/rest/services/MarineChart_Services/NOAACharts/MapServer/WMTS" rel="noopener"
                                 target="_blank">NOAA Chart Display Service (Web Map Tile Service (WMTS))</a>
                                                      </div>
                                                      <div class="small">
                              TMS - Tile Map Service
                            </div>
                                                                                <div class="small">
                                    <p>The NOAA Chart Display Service renders NOAA ENC data with &quot;traditional paper chart&quot; symbols, labels, and color schemes familiar to those who have used NOAA paper nautical charts or the NOAA Custom Chart application. This is the Web Map Tile Service. </p>
                              </div>
                                                  </li>
                                                <li>
                          <div class="force-break">
