    <td class="ellipsisize">
              2001
          </td>
  </tr>
                              <tr>
    <th scope="col">Abstract:</th>
    <td class="small">
            <p>The Office of Coast Survey (OCS) has been involved in the development of a NOAA Electronic Navigational Chart (NOAA ENC) suite to support the marine transportation infrastructure and coastal management for a number of years. The NOAA ENC will support all types of marine navigation by providing the official database for electronic charting systems (ECS), including the Electronic Chart Display and Information System (ECDIS). NOAA ENCs support real-time navigation as well as collision and grounding avoidance needs of the mariner, and accommodate a real-time tide and current display capability that is essential for large vessel navigation.  NOAA ENCs will also provide fully integrated vector base maps for use in geographic information systems (GIS) that are used for coastal management or other purposes. The NOAA ENCs are in the International Hydrographic Office (IHO) S-57 international exchange format and comply with the ENC Product Specification.</p>
      </td>
  </tr>
                  <tr>
    <th scope="col">Purpose:</th>
    <td class="small">
            <p>The electronic navigational charts (NOAA ENC) are primarily intended to support the navigation of vessels in the territorial waters of the United States.  The data contained in the NOAA ENCs may also be used for any other coastal mapping purposes that require up-to-date information similar to that portrayed on traditional navigational charts.</p>
      </td>
  </tr>
                  <tr>
    <th scope="col">Notes:</th>
    <td class="small">
            <p>1530</p>
      </td>
  </tr>
                                                                                        </table>
        </div>
      </div> <!-- .section Item Identification -->

